      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5438_Start6" name="Onboarding; recurring awareness cycle; insider-threat signal (VS-125/VS-119)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5438_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5438_Task7" name="Run OT-specific cyber awareness for engineering/maintenance staff and vendors —…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Run OT-specific cyber awareness for engineering/maintenance staff and vendors — why a USB in a controller engineering workstation or a default password is catastrophic, not just an IT issue.
Responsible (R): OT Security Analyst / L&amp;D
Accountable (A): OT Security Lead
Duration: annual + onboarding</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5438_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5438_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5438_Task8" name="Lock down OT engineering workstations — no general internet/email, host-based…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Lock down OT engineering workstations — no general internet/email, host-based protection, removable-media control, and clean-before-connect for any field laptop.
Responsible (R): OT Security Engineer
Accountable (A): OT Security Lead
Duration: continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5438_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5438_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5438_Task9" name="Apply insider-threat controls to OT-privileged users (detect mass config…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Apply insider-threat controls to OT-privileged users (detect mass config export, off-hours controller access, credential abuse) coordinated with VS-125/VS-119.
Responsible (R): OT SOC Analyst
Accountable (A): OT Security Lead
Duration: continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5438_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5438_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5438_Task10" name="Ensure contingent/vendor personnel (VS-98/VS-167) get OT-aware vetting and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Ensure contingent/vendor personnel (VS-98/VS-167) get OT-aware vetting and access commensurate with the OT-criticality tier they touch.
Responsible (R): OT Security Lead / VS-167
Accountable (A): OT Security Lead
Duration: per onboarding</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5438_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5438_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5438_Task11" name="Reinforce with documented sanctions/escalation paths (HR VS-84/VS-103, Legal…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Reinforce with documented sanctions/escalation paths (HR VS-84/VS-103, Legal VS-100) for OT security policy violations.
Responsible (R): OT Security Lead
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5438_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5438_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5438_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5438_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5438_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-802 (ensure controlled execution — OT Compliance, Third-Party Access &amp; Cyber Resilience Analytics (PA-190.3).) | - operational: least privilege / workstation hygiene; awareness and insider-risk controls; no general internet/email on OT engineering workstations.
Owner: OT Security Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
